{
  "raw": {
    "https://opsu.edu/job-opportunities/": {
      "title": "Job Opportunities",
      "description": "Job Opportunities – Oklahoma Panhandle State University Oklahoma Panhandle State University Admissions & Aid Office of Recruitment Recruitment Applying to OPSU Visits & Tours New Student Orientation Admissions and Academic Records Office of the Registrar Advising and Enrollment Graduation & Commencement Transcript Requests FERPA Paying for College Tuition & Fees Scholarships Financial Aid Bursar Net Price Calculator Academics Colleges Agriculture, Science & Nursing Arts & Education Business & Technology General Information General Catalog Academic Calendar New Aggie Orientation Honors & Awards Student Outcomes Student Services Academic Resource Center Marvin E. McKee Library Hispanic Student Center Aggie Writing Center Online Learning Readiness Online Bookstore Aggie Life Life on Campus University Student Housing Dining on Campus Safety & Security Student Engagement Campus Organizations What’s Happening Events News Panhandle Magazine Aggie Fan Store About OPSU Get to Know Us About the University Strategic Plan Leadership Safety & Security Communications Our Campus Visits & Tours Campus Map Offices & Facilities Directory Careers What We Stand For Policies & Procedures Accessibility Accreditation Consumer Information Athletics Apply Visit Request Information Search OPSU Close Search OPSU Office of Recruitment Admissions and Academic Records Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Ways to Give myOPSU Portal Apply to OPSU News Careers Request Information Athletics Aggie Access Directory Follow OPSU on Instagram Follow OPSU on Facebook Follow OPSU on X Job Opportunities Career Opportunities Thank you for your interest in employment with Oklahoma Panhandle State University. If you are applying for more than one position, please submit a separate application for each position, being sure that your cover letter addresses the specific requirements for the position for which you are applying. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Program Facilitator/Upward Bound Program The main objective of the Upward Bound at OPSU program is preparing rural high school students who are economically disadvantaged and/or potential first-generation college students for entrance into and persistence in postsecondary education. The Program Facilitator reports to the Director of the program. Position Type 12-month, Grant funded position; annual renewal contingent upon continued grant funding Job Details Assistant Athletic Trainer To assist with the supervision and coordination of the University’s overall athletic training program, including, but not limited to: injury prevention, evaluation, management, and treatment of athletic injuries, short-term and long rehabilitation of athletic injuries, with and under the supervision of the Head Athletic Trainer, Team Physician, and other qualified medical personnel. Position Type Full Time, 12 Months Job Details Carpenter Performs routine preventative maintenance on equipment and assists skilled maintenance workers in repairing machinery, plumbing, physical structures and electrical wiring fixtures. Position Type Full Time, 12 Months Job Details Assistant Women’s Soccer Coach Assist the head coach with supervision and coordination of the soccer program. Start date: August 1, 2026 Position Type Part Time, 10 months Job Details USSR Hourly- General Maintenance Worker Performs routine preventative maintenance on equipment and assists in repairing machinery, plumbing, physical structures and fixtures. Position Type Full-time or Part-time Job Details USSR Hourly- Grounds Maintenance Worker Standard horticultural and grounds keeping practices; the use and maintenance of grounds keeping tools and equipment.  Performs a variety of grounds maintenance and gardening duties and assists in related various construction and landscaping projects. Position Type Full-time or Part-time Job Details Background Checks OPSU conducts background checks for applicants being considered for employment. Background checks include a criminal background check and sex offender registry check. For certain positions, there may also be a financial (credit) background check and/or a Motor Vehicle Registry (MVR) check. A criminal conviction or arrest pending adjudication or adverse financial history information alone shall not disqualify an applicant in the absence of a relationship to the requirements of the position. Background check information will be used in a confidential, non-discriminatory manner consistent with state and federal law. OPSU is an AA/EE/E-Verify employer committed to diversity. Oklahoma Panhandle State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, and veterans status in its programs and services. Files & Forms Summary of Your Rights Non-discrimination Policy Inquiries The following persons have been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies. Please contact Robert Crawley regarding Section 504/ADA (disabilities). Please contact Cheyenne Heltzel regarding discrimination (race, color, national origin, age, and veteran status) and Title IX (sex). Contact Human Resources Address Oklahoma Panhandle State University Office of Human Resources P.O. Box 430 Goodwell, OK 73939 Phone (580) 349-2611 Fax (580) 349-2302 Email opsu.jobs@opsu.edu About Admissions Academics Aggie Life Applying to OPSU Visits Request Information myOPSU Portal Make a Payment Directory Library Bookstore Athletics Safety & Security Aggie Access Careers Information Technology Privacy Policy Terms of Service Title IX EthicsPoint Health, Safety, and Well-being Address P.O. Box 430 • Goodwell, OK 73939 Phone (580) 349-2611 Toll-free (800) 664-OPSU Contact Contact us online"
    },
    "https://opsu.edu/jobs/program-facilitator-upward-bound-program/": {
      "title": "Program Facilitator/Upward Bound Program",
      "description": "Program Facilitator/Upward Bound Program – Oklahoma Panhandle State University Oklahoma Panhandle State University Admissions & Aid Office of Recruitment Recruitment Applying to OPSU Visits & Tours New Student Orientation Admissions and Academic Records Office of the Registrar Advising and Enrollment Graduation & Commencement Transcript Requests FERPA Paying for College Tuition & Fees Scholarships Financial Aid Bursar Net Price Calculator Academics Colleges Agriculture, Science & Nursing Arts & Education Business & Technology General Information General Catalog Academic Calendar New Aggie Orientation Honors & Awards Student Outcomes Student Services Academic Resource Center Marvin E. McKee Library Hispanic Student Center Aggie Writing Center Online Learning Readiness Online Bookstore Aggie Life Life on Campus University Student Housing Dining on Campus Safety & Security Student Engagement Campus Organizations What’s Happening Events News Panhandle Magazine Aggie Fan Store About OPSU Get to Know Us About the University Strategic Plan Leadership Safety & Security Communications Our Campus Visits & Tours Campus Map Offices & Facilities Directory Careers What We Stand For Policies & Procedures Accessibility Accreditation Consumer Information Athletics Apply Visit Request Information Search OPSU Close Search OPSU Office of Recruitment Admissions and Academic Records Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Ways to Give myOPSU Portal Apply to OPSU News Careers Request Information Athletics Aggie Access Directory Follow OPSU on Instagram Follow OPSU on Facebook Follow OPSU on X Program Facilitator/Upward Bound Program Start Date October 5, 2026 Listed On September 3, 2026 Position Type 12-month, Grant funded position; annual renewal contingent upon continued grant funding Salary $40,000-$44,000 Job Summary The main objective of the Upward Bound at OPSU program is preparing rural high school students who are economically disadvantaged and/or potential first-generation college students for entrance into and persistence in postsecondary education. The Program Facilitator reports to the Director of the program. Responsibilities Recruit and screen program participants and provide individual counseling services at target high schools. Monitor student academic progress and consult with high school staff. Analyze and screen student applications and family financial data for program eligibility. Coordinate instructional/tutorial services for weekly sessions at individual target schools. Review and analyze student academic records for academic deficiencies and coordinate remedial services; monitor student academic progress and revise educational plan as required. Maintain up-to-date project and individual counseling records and assist with other data collection as required. Provide effective personal, academic, career and financial aid counseling to program participants at target high schools and on OPSU campus. Plan and execute quarterly cultural events for program participants. Travel to target schools to provide project services. Coordinate student tutors for assisting at target schools. Plan and execute group presentations on postsecondary entrance requirements, ACT preparation, financial aid, study skills and other relevant topics. Assist Director with extensive planning for and coordination of 6-week summer residential component for program participants on OPSU’s campus. Participate in staff/professional development and professional organizations, which promote educational opportunity/access. Provide leadership in Director’s absence. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Ability to provide comprehensive counseling services which result in participants enrolling in postsecondary education. Ability to operate a personal computer and necessary software applications. Ability to input and track student information and progress using Excel and Student Access programs. Ability to effectively plan and execute program activities assigned by the Director. Ability to work effectively with target school staff to identify potential participants and coordinate program services. Ability to advocate for first-generation and/or low-income program participants seeking postsecondary education. Ability to work Saturdays as needed during academic year and evenings during the Summer Session. Ability to interact in an effective and appropriate manner with diverse populations, the University community and the public. Ability to communicate effectively. Ability to maintain confidentiality. Ability to relate effectively to students and parents and demonstrate sensitivity to the special needs of target population; Ability to work independently, meet deadlines and manage multiple assignments. Ability to travel extensively to target schools. Ability to lift 50 pounds required for the loading, transporting, and unloading of supplies. Ability to transfer supplies as needed to participant locations. Must possess valid Oklahoma Driver 's License for the transportation of students along with other necessary driving requirements as set by the State of Oklahoma. Ability to spend lengthy time riding/driving with extensive travel to target schools. Ability to safely transport program participants in University vehicles. Requires commitment, long hours and a high energy level. Ability to safely transport program participants in University vehicles. Ability to transfer supplies as needed to participant locations. Must have a strong work ethic and lead by example. Must be a professional, credible and respected representative of the institution internally and in the community Demonstrated willingness and ability to act ethically and socially responsible Can be exposed to a variety of weather conditions for periods of time. Ability to communicate in a courteous manner Other duties as assigned by Director of Upward Bound or designee. Qualifications Bilingual in English and Spanish Previous experience working with disadvantaged high school youth. Previous TRIO experience Bachelor' s degree required. Three years of previous experience in education, counseling, social work, or related area. A background check will be required of the successful applicant. About Oklahoma Panhandle State University (OPSU): OPSU is regionally accredited by the Higher Learning Commission and is the first public Hispanic Serving Institution in Oklahoma. The university is a baccalaureate degree granting institution located in Goodwell, Oklahoma. Rooted in “Progress through Knowledge,” OPSU is committed to promoting excellence in the preparation of students for success in a global community. Our university achieved multiple rankings by the 2023 U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings: #3 Best Value Regional Colleges West; #8 Top Public Colleges for the Western Region; and #17 Best Regional Colleges West. U.S New and World Report also recognized OPSU as one of the top ten universities in Oklahoma, standing out of our affordable tuition rates. Apply Now Applicant must submit: Letter of Application Resume Three Reference, current addresses and phone numbers All unofficial transcripts Self- Identification of Disability Form Self- Identification of Veterans Form About Admissions Academics Aggie Life Applying to OPSU Visits Request Information myOPSU Portal Make a Payment Directory Library Bookstore Athletics Safety & Security Aggie Access Careers Information Technology Privacy Policy Terms of Service Title IX EthicsPoint Health, Safety, and Well-being Address P.O. Box 430 • Goodwell, OK 73939 Phone (580) 349-2611 Toll-free (800) 664-OPSU Contact Contact us online"
    },
    "https://opsu.edu/jobs/assistant-athletic-trainer/": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Assistant Athletic Trainer – Oklahoma Panhandle State University Oklahoma Panhandle State University Admissions & Aid Office of Recruitment Recruitment Applying to OPSU Visits & Tours New Student Orientation Admissions and Academic Records Office of the Registrar Advising and Enrollment Graduation & Commencement Transcript Requests FERPA Paying for College Tuition & Fees Scholarships Financial Aid Bursar Net Price Calculator Academics Colleges Agriculture, Science & Nursing Arts & Education Business & Technology General Information General Catalog Academic Calendar New Aggie Orientation Honors & Awards Student Outcomes Student Services Academic Resource Center Marvin E. McKee Library Hispanic Student Center Aggie Writing Center Online Learning Readiness Online Bookstore Aggie Life Life on Campus University Student Housing Dining on Campus Safety & Security Student Engagement Campus Organizations What’s Happening Events News Panhandle Magazine Aggie Fan Store About OPSU Get to Know Us About the University Strategic Plan Leadership Safety & Security Communications Our Campus Visits & Tours Campus Map Offices & Facilities Directory Careers What We Stand For Policies & Procedures Accessibility Accreditation Consumer Information Athletics Apply Visit Request Information Search OPSU Close Search OPSU Office of Recruitment Admissions and Academic Records Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Ways to Give myOPSU Portal Apply to OPSU News Careers Request Information Athletics Aggie Access Directory Follow OPSU on Instagram Follow OPSU on Facebook Follow OPSU on X Assistant Athletic Trainer Start Date July 20, 2026 Listed On July 6, 2026 Position Type Full Time, 12 Months Salary $34,000 + $8,050 adjunct pay Job Summary To assist with the supervision and coordination of the University’s overall athletic training program, including, but not limited to: injury prevention, evaluation, management, and treatment of athletic injuries, short-term and long rehabilitation of athletic injuries, with and under the supervision of the Head Athletic Trainer, Team Physician, and other qualified medical personnel. Responsibilities Provide treatment, assessment, and rehabilitation of all injured athletes as the primary or secondary athletic trainer for specific teams assigned by the Head Athletic Trainer, including attendance at scheduled team practices and home and away competitions as necessary Electronic documentation of all athletic training medical records and injuries Oversees the daily management of training room, including ordering and storage of supplies and equipment Provide accommodation recommendations, related to sports, for student-athletes with restrictions or limitations Makes appropriate physician’s referrals and appointments Communicate with physicians, specialist, parents, and coaching staff regarding the injury status of athletes Monitor weather conditions and dangerous environments Organizes and administers drug testing per department policy Responsible for administrative and other work-related duties as assigned Must have a strong work ethic and lead by example. Must be a professional, credible and respected representative of the institution internally and in the community. Demonstrated willingness and ability to act ethically and socially responsible. Must be able to lift more than 100-lb. objects; frequent bending, stooping, and   walking. Must have the ability to organize, prioritize, and perform multiple tasks with little or no supervision. Ability to communicate in a courteous manner. Ability to work a flexible schedule, including evenings, weekends, and holidays. Can be exposed to a variety of weather conditions for periods of time. Qualifications Master’s degree in Athletic Training or related field. Certification by the National Athletic Trainer’s Association Board of Certification (NATABOC). Oklahoma licensure by the State Office of Allied Health Professions or eligible for such licensure. NPI Number Required. About Oklahoma Panhandle State University (OPSU): OPSU is regionally accredited by the Higher Learning Commission and is the first public Hispanic Serving Institution in Oklahoma. The university is a baccalaureate degree granting institution located in Goodwell, Oklahoma. Rooted in “Progress through Knowledge,” OPSU is committed to promoting excellence in the preparation of students for success in a global community. Our university achieved multiple rankings by the 2023 U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings: #3 Best Value Regional Colleges West; #8 Top Public Colleges for the Western Region; and #17 Best Regional Colleges West. U.S New and World Report also recognized OPSU as one of the top ten universities in Oklahoma, standing out of our affordable tuition rates. Apply Now Applicant must submit: Letter of Application Resume Three Reference, current addresses and phone numbers All unofficial transcripts Self- Identification of Disability Form Self- Identification of Veterans Form About Admissions Academics Aggie Life Applying to OPSU Visits Request Information myOPSU Portal Make a Payment Directory Library Bookstore Athletics Safety & Security Aggie Access Careers Information Technology Privacy Policy Terms of Service Title IX EthicsPoint Health, Safety, and Well-being Address P.O. Box 430 • Goodwell, OK 73939 Phone (580) 349-2611 Toll-free (800) 664-OPSU Contact Contact us online"
    },
    "https://opsu.edu/jobs/carpenter/": {
      "title": "Carpenter",
      "description": "Carpenter – Oklahoma Panhandle State University Oklahoma Panhandle State University Admissions & Aid Office of Recruitment Recruitment Applying to OPSU Visits & Tours New Student Orientation Admissions and Academic Records Office of the Registrar Advising and Enrollment Graduation & Commencement Transcript Requests FERPA Paying for College Tuition & Fees Scholarships Financial Aid Bursar Net Price Calculator Academics Colleges Agriculture, Science & Nursing Arts & Education Business & Technology General Information General Catalog Academic Calendar New Aggie Orientation Honors & Awards Student Outcomes Student Services Academic Resource Center Marvin E. McKee Library Hispanic Student Center Aggie Writing Center Online Learning Readiness Online Bookstore Aggie Life Life on Campus University Student Housing Dining on Campus Safety & Security Student Engagement Campus Organizations What’s Happening Events News Panhandle Magazine Aggie Fan Store About OPSU Get to Know Us About the University Strategic Plan Leadership Safety & Security Communications Our Campus Visits & Tours Campus Map Offices & Facilities Directory Careers What We Stand For Policies & Procedures Accessibility Accreditation Consumer Information Athletics Apply Visit Request Information Search OPSU Close Search OPSU Office of Recruitment Admissions and Academic Records Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Ways to Give myOPSU Portal Apply to OPSU News Careers Request Information Athletics Aggie Access Directory Follow OPSU on Instagram Follow OPSU on Facebook Follow OPSU on X Carpenter Start Date July 31, 2026 Listed On June 24, 2026 Position Type Full Time, 12 Months Salary $30,000-$33,000 Job Summary Performs routine preventative maintenance on equipment and assists skilled maintenance workers in repairing machinery, plumbing, physical structures and electrical wiring fixtures. Responsibilities Bends and cuts conduit, cuts wires and drills holes in wall, floors or ceilings for electrical connection. Connects wires to motors, fixtures and other electrical equipment, replaces switches and fuses, and splices wires and insulates wires with friction tape. Bends, cuts and threads pipe, cuts opening in walls, ceiling and floors for pipes and seals pipe joints. Dismantles machine or equipment, replaces defective parts and motors and adjusts feed mechanisms. Performs routine maintenance on machines, such as cleaning and lubricating shafts, pulleys, gear and bearings, using rags, brushes, grease gun and oil can. Cuts out and joins parts for worktables, benches, shelves and other furnishings, using hand-tools and materials, such as saws, hammers, nails and screws. Paints walls, ceilings or fixtures of building. Assists university painter in preparing surfaces for painting and pre-masking of paint areas. Replaces filters and belts in building equipment rooms. Performs campus rounds, on weekends, when assigned, checking to ensure water systems, sewer systems, and building equipment is operating properly. May perform a variety of other duties to include moving of furniture, material, and equipment. Must have a strong work ethic and lead by example. Must be a professional, credible and respected representative of the institution internally and in the community Demonstrated willingness and ability to act ethically and socially responsible Must be able to lift more than 50-lb. objects; frequent bending, stooping, and   walking. Can be exposed to a variety of weather conditions for periods of time. Ability to communicate in a courteous manner Other duties as assigned by Vice President of Fiscal Affairs or his/her designee. Qualifications EDUCATION, TRAINING AND EXPERIENCE:\r\nRequired: Two years maintenance experience Ability to understand the following directions as given. Two years maintenance experience. Must have current Oklahoma State driver’s license. Ability to read labels and instruction for proper use of chemicals and equipment. Ability to use a variety of hand power tools. The ability to lift 60 pounds, ability to work from ladders or raised platforms. About Oklahoma Panhandle State University (OPSU): OPSU is regionally accredited by the Higher Learning Commission and is the first public Hispanic Serving Institution in Oklahoma. The university is a baccalaureate degree granting institution located in Goodwell, Oklahoma. Rooted in “Progress through Knowledge,” OPSU is committed to promoting excellence in the preparation of students for success in a global community. Our university achieved multiple rankings by the 2023 U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings: #3 Best Value Regional Colleges West; #8 Top Public Colleges for the Western Region; and #17 Best Regional Colleges West. U.S New and World Report also recognized OPSU as one of the top ten universities in Oklahoma, standing out of our affordable tuition rates. Apply Now Applicant must submit: Letter of Application Resume Three Reference, current addresses and phone numbers All unofficial transcripts Self- Identification of Disability Form Self- Identification of Veterans Form About Admissions Academics Aggie Life Applying to OPSU Visits Request Information myOPSU Portal Make a Payment Directory Library Bookstore Athletics Safety & Security Aggie Access Careers Information Technology Privacy Policy Terms of Service Title IX EthicsPoint Health, Safety, and Well-being Address P.O. Box 430 • Goodwell, OK 73939 Phone (580) 349-2611 Toll-free (800) 664-OPSU Contact Contact us online"
    },
    "https://opsu.edu/jobs/assistant-womens-soccer-coach/": {
      "title": "Assistant Women's Soccer Coach",
      "description": "Assistant Women’s Soccer Coach – Oklahoma Panhandle State University Oklahoma Panhandle State University Admissions & Aid Office of Recruitment Recruitment Applying to OPSU Visits & Tours New Student Orientation Admissions and Academic Records Office of the Registrar Advising and Enrollment Graduation & Commencement Transcript Requests FERPA Paying for College Tuition & Fees Scholarships Financial Aid Bursar Net Price Calculator Academics Colleges Agriculture, Science & Nursing Arts & Education Business & Technology General Information General Catalog Academic Calendar New Aggie Orientation Honors & Awards Student Outcomes Student Services Academic Resource Center Marvin E. McKee Library Hispanic Student Center Aggie Writing Center Online Learning Readiness Online Bookstore Aggie Life Life on Campus University Student Housing Dining on Campus Safety & Security Student Engagement Campus Organizations What’s Happening Events News Panhandle Magazine Aggie Fan Store About OPSU Get to Know Us About the University Strategic Plan Leadership Safety & Security Communications Our Campus Visits & Tours Campus Map Offices & Facilities Directory Careers What We Stand For Policies & Procedures Accessibility Accreditation Consumer Information Athletics Apply Visit Request Information Search OPSU Close Search OPSU Office of Recruitment Admissions and Academic Records Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Ways to Give myOPSU Portal Apply to OPSU News Careers Request Information Athletics Aggie Access Directory Follow OPSU on Instagram Follow OPSU on Facebook Follow OPSU on X Assistant Women's Soccer Coach Start Date August 1, 2026 Listed On May 14, 2026 Position Type Part Time, 10 months Salary $15,000 Job Summary Assist the head coach with supervision and coordination of the soccer program. Start date: August 1, 2026 Responsibilities Assist in developing and executing recruitment of quality student athletes including but not limited to:  off-campus evaluation, contacts, organization of on-campus visits, and tryouts. Advise and instruct student-athletes on skill development. Be an integral part of practice and game preparation. Attend and instruct during all games, practices, weightlifting sessions, conditioning sessions, and individual workouts. Develop and implement an academic monitoring system of all student-athletes. Organize and carry out film exchanges through Game Tape Exchange. Organization and burning of game film for opponents and head coach. Develop and implement a strength program. Monitoring the student-athletes’ growth within the strength program. Scouting of opponents and instructing team on the strategies that will be implemented. Liaison for the program with the Athletic Training Staff. Equipment and gear maintenance. Advise student-athletes in their day to day activities. Maintain a good working relationship with all athletic coaches and staff regarding facility use and condition. Other duties assigned by the Head Coach. Must be able to lift more than 50-lb. objects; frequent bending, stooping, and   walking. Ability to work various hours, including nights and weekends throughout the year for practice, games and recruiting. Be able to transport team to the contests, and be responsible for their well-being. Could be exposed to a variety of weather conditions. Other duties as assigned by the Athletic Director or his/her designee Qualifications EDUCATION, TRAINING AND EXPERIENCE:  Bachelor’s degree; master’s degree preferred Previous successful coaching experience. College coaching and/or playing experience and recruiting at the collegiate level preferred. Ability to work various hours, including nights and weekends throughout the year for practice, games and recruiting. Excellent written/oral communication, as well as demonstrate strong organizational skills. About Oklahoma Panhandle State University (OPSU): OPSU is regionally accredited by the Higher Learning Commission and is the first public Hispanic Serving Institution in Oklahoma. The university is a baccalaureate degree granting institution located in Goodwell, Oklahoma. Rooted in “Progress through Knowledge,” OPSU is committed to promoting excellence in the preparation of students for success in a global community. Our university achieved multiple rankings by the 2023 U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings: #3 Best Value Regional Colleges West; #8 Top Public Colleges for the Western Region; and #17 Best Regional Colleges West. U.S New and World Report also recognized OPSU as one of the top ten universities in Oklahoma, standing out of our affordable tuition rates. Apply Now Applicant must submit: Letter of Application Resume Three Reference, current addresses and phone numbers All unofficial transcripts Self- Identification of Disability Form Self- Identification of Veterans Form About Admissions Academics Aggie Life Applying to OPSU Visits Request Information myOPSU Portal Make a Payment Directory Library Bookstore Athletics Safety & Security Aggie Access Careers Information Technology Privacy Policy Terms of Service Title IX EthicsPoint Health, Safety, and Well-being Address P.O. Box 430 • Goodwell, OK 73939 Phone (580) 349-2611 Toll-free (800) 664-OPSU Contact Contact us online"
    },
    "https://opsu.edu/jobs/ussr-hourly-general-maintenance-worker/": {
      "title": "USSR Hourly- General Maintenance Worker",
      "description": "USSR Hourly- General Maintenance Worker – Oklahoma Panhandle State University Oklahoma Panhandle State University Admissions & Aid Office of Recruitment Recruitment Applying to OPSU Visits & Tours New Student Orientation Admissions and Academic Records Office of the Registrar Advising and Enrollment Graduation & Commencement Transcript Requests FERPA Paying for College Tuition & Fees Scholarships Financial Aid Bursar Net Price Calculator Academics Colleges Agriculture, Science & Nursing Arts & Education Business & Technology General Information General Catalog Academic Calendar New Aggie Orientation Honors & Awards Student Outcomes Student Services Academic Resource Center Marvin E. McKee Library Hispanic Student Center Aggie Writing Center Online Learning Readiness Online Bookstore Aggie Life Life on Campus University Student Housing Dining on Campus Safety & Security Student Engagement Campus Organizations What’s Happening Events News Panhandle Magazine Aggie Fan Store About OPSU Get to Know Us About the University Strategic Plan Leadership Safety & Security Communications Our Campus Visits & Tours Campus Map Offices & Facilities Directory Careers What We Stand For Policies & Procedures Accessibility Accreditation Consumer Information Athletics Apply Visit Request Information Search OPSU Close Search OPSU Office of Recruitment Admissions and Academic Records Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Ways to Give myOPSU Portal Apply to OPSU News Careers Request Information Athletics Aggie Access Directory Follow OPSU on Instagram Follow OPSU on Facebook Follow OPSU on X USSR Hourly- General Maintenance Worker Start Date October 1, 2025 Listed On September 23, 2025 Position Type Full-time or Part-time Salary Hourly Job Summary Performs routine preventative maintenance on equipment and assists in repairing machinery, plumbing, physical structures and fixtures. Responsibilities Bends and cuts conduit, cuts wires and drills holes in wall, floors or ceilings for electrical connection. Connects wires to motors, fixtures and other electrical equipment, replaces switches and fuses, and splices wires and insulates wires with friction tape, if not required by a certified electrician. Bends, cuts and threads pipe, cuts opening in walls, ceiling and floors for pipes and seals pipe joints. Dismantles machine or equipment, replaces defective parts and motors and adjusts feed mechanisms. Performs routine maintenance on machines, such as cleaning and lubricating shafts, pulleys, gear and bearings, using rags, brushes, grease gun and oil can. Cuts out and joins parts for worktables, benches, shelves and other furnishings, using hand-tools and materials, such as saws, hammers, nails and screws. Paints walls, ceilings or fixtures of building. Prepares surfaces for painting and pre-masking of paint areas. Replaces filters and belts in building equipment rooms. May perform a variety of other duties to include moving of furniture, material, and equipment. Must have a strong work ethic and lead by example. Must be a professional, credible and respected representative of the institution internally and in the community Demonstrated willingness and ability to act ethically and socially responsible Must be able to lift more than 50-lb. objects; frequent bending, stooping, and walking. Can be exposed to a variety of weather conditions for periods of time. Ability to communicate in a courteous manner Other duties as assigned by Vice President of Fiscal Affairs or his/her designee. Qualifications Ability to understand the following directions as given. Two years maintenance experience. Must have current Oklahoma State driver’s license. Ability to read labels and instruction for proper use of chemicals and equipment. Ability to use a variety of hand power tools. The ability to lift 60 pounds, ability to work from ladders or raised platforms. Experience preferred. About Oklahoma Panhandle State University (OPSU): OPSU is regionally accredited by the Higher Learning Commission and is the first public Hispanic Serving Institution in Oklahoma. The university is a baccalaureate degree granting institution located in Goodwell, Oklahoma. Rooted in “Progress through Knowledge,” OPSU is committed to promoting excellence in the preparation of students for success in a global community. Our university achieved multiple rankings by the 2023 U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings: #3 Best Value Regional Colleges West; #8 Top Public Colleges for the Western Region; and #17 Best Regional Colleges West. U.S New and World Report also recognized OPSU as one of the top ten universities in Oklahoma, standing out of our affordable tuition rates. Apply Now Applicant must submit: About Admissions Academics Aggie Life Applying to OPSU Visits Request Information myOPSU Portal Make a Payment Directory Library Bookstore Athletics Safety & Security Aggie Access Careers Information Technology Privacy Policy Terms of Service Title IX EthicsPoint Health, Safety, and Well-being Address P.O. Box 430 • Goodwell, OK 73939 Phone (580) 349-2611 Toll-free (800) 664-OPSU Contact Contact us online"
    },
    "https://opsu.edu/jobs/ussr-hourly-grounds-maintenance-worker/": {
      "title": "USSR Hourly- Grounds Maintenance Worker",
      "description": "USSR Hourly- Grounds Maintenance Worker – Oklahoma Panhandle State University Oklahoma Panhandle State University Admissions & Aid Office of Recruitment Recruitment Applying to OPSU Visits & Tours New Student Orientation Admissions and Academic Records Office of the Registrar Advising and Enrollment Graduation & Commencement Transcript Requests FERPA Paying for College Tuition & Fees Scholarships Financial Aid Bursar Net Price Calculator Academics Colleges Agriculture, Science & Nursing Arts & Education Business & Technology General Information General Catalog Academic Calendar New Aggie Orientation Honors & Awards Student Outcomes Student Services Academic Resource Center Marvin E. McKee Library Hispanic Student Center Aggie Writing Center Online Learning Readiness Online Bookstore Aggie Life Life on Campus University Student Housing Dining on Campus Safety & Security Student Engagement Campus Organizations What’s Happening Events News Panhandle Magazine Aggie Fan Store About OPSU Get to Know Us About the University Strategic Plan Leadership Safety & Security Communications Our Campus Visits & Tours Campus Map Offices & Facilities Directory Careers What We Stand For Policies & Procedures Accessibility Accreditation Consumer Information Athletics Apply Visit Request Information Search OPSU Close Search OPSU Office of Recruitment Admissions and Academic Records Parents & Families Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Ways to Give myOPSU Portal Apply to OPSU News Careers Request Information Athletics Aggie Access Directory Follow OPSU on Instagram Follow OPSU on Facebook Follow OPSU on X USSR Hourly- Grounds Maintenance Worker Start Date October 1, 2025 Listed On September 23, 2025 Position Type Full-time or Part-time Salary Hourly Job Summary Standard horticultural and grounds keeping practices; the use and maintenance of grounds keeping tools and equipment.  Performs a variety of grounds maintenance and gardening duties and assists in related various construction and landscaping projects. Responsibilities At the direction of the Director of Physical Plant, maintains and cares for campus grounds. Maintains and cares for the mowing of University grounds with hand and power mowers, edging and weed eating, weeding beds, pruning trees and trimming hedges to promote growth and improve appearance. May apply fertilizers and weed control chemicals as directed by Director of Physical Plant. Connects sprinkling equipment and waters lawns, athletic fields, and flower beds. Adjusts and repairs such equipment as lawnmowers, sprinklers, and hedge shears. Inspects flowers, shrubs, trees, and lawns for evidence of insects, fungi and other pests and reports to Director of Physical Plant. Collects and disposes of leaves and refuse. During winter, assists in the plowing of snow from sidewalks, driveways, and playgrounds, and spreads sand or salt as needed. Supervises the repair of outdoor facilities. Other duties as assigned by the Director of Physical Plant or his/her designee. Must have a strong work ethic and lead by example. Must be a professional, credible and respected representative of the institution internally and in the community Demonstrated willingness and ability to act ethically and socially responsible Must be able to lift more than 50-lb. objects; frequent bending, stooping, and   walking. Can be exposed to a variety of weather conditions for periods of time. Ability to communicate in a courteous manner Other duties as assigned by Vice President of Fiscal Affairs or his/her designee. Qualifications Experience preferred. About Oklahoma Panhandle State University (OPSU): OPSU is regionally accredited by the Higher Learning Commission and is the first public Hispanic Serving Institution in Oklahoma. The university is a baccalaureate degree granting institution located in Goodwell, Oklahoma. Rooted in “Progress through Knowledge,” OPSU is committed to promoting excellence in the preparation of students for success in a global community. Our university achieved multiple rankings by the 2023 U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings: #3 Best Value Regional Colleges West; #8 Top Public Colleges for the Western Region; and #17 Best Regional Colleges West. U.S New and World Report also recognized OPSU as one of the top ten universities in Oklahoma, standing out of our affordable tuition rates. Apply Now Applicant must submit: About Admissions Academics Aggie Life Applying to OPSU Visits Request Information myOPSU Portal Make a Payment Directory Library Bookstore Athletics Safety & Security Aggie Access Careers Information Technology Privacy Policy Terms of Service Title IX EthicsPoint Health, Safety, and Well-being Address P.O. Box 430 • Goodwell, OK 73939 Phone (580) 349-2611 Toll-free (800) 664-OPSU Contact Contact us online"
    }
